       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg at once is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily**, a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Something else.** If the 1600 mg figure is correct, please confirm it and tell me the indication. I can then add a note to the order, though it may still need pharmacist or prescriber review.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
