     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is well past any recognized dosing limit, and I can't find a clinical scenario where that dose would help this patient more than it would harm them. The risks include GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your documentation wouldn't reduce that risk for the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg or 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily**, if you want a lower dose.\n\nIf you need more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than those give, a pharmacist or the attending can help with a multimodal regimen. That might add scheduled acetaminophen or use a different agent.\n\nIf you think there's a real exception, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, please take it to pharmacy or the attending. They can place or verify the order through the proper channel. Tell me which of the doses above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
